  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This feature is simple – you can clone yourself in multiple/different avatars\nThe ability to create an animated clone of your avatar that replicates all of your movements locally(only you can see it). It features a \"Record\" option in the radial menu that allows you to record your motions indefinitely and a \"Stop Recording\" option that allows you to create an animation that plays indefinitely until removed. The clone includes toggles, visemes, blend shapes and physbones interactivity.\nThe ability to create a frozen clone of your avatar that replicates your exact pose. You can either set a timer or hit a button to instantly clone yourself.\nThe capability to add an unlimited or limited number of clones, including the ability to remove clones individually or by \"first created\" or \"last created\" in their radial menu.\nThe ability to view cloned avatars through the camera.\nIf you change your avatar the clone's avatar will stay the same.\nThe viewing of cloned avatars is local by default, but you can choose to show specific friends clones.\nWhat are the benefits of This?\nThis will benefit avatar creators by enabling them to effortlessly inspect their avatars for issues. It also benefits everyone by allowing them to view their avatars from all angles, including the back.\nIt makes it possible to create higher-quality VRChat content (video, projects, and filmmaking production) conveniently and efficiently.\nIt allows VRChat Players to assess their movements in real time from a third-person perspective. \nWho benefits from this?\nHere’s who this feature benefits:\nContent Creators\nPhotography Enthusiasts\nAvatar Creators\nThe player base\nThis was originally a mod known as Freezeframe (https://github.com/Er1807/FreezeFrame) that many at the time utilized to make amazing groundbreaking creative videos/photos that otherwise wouldn’t be possible, or would require many players. \nThis will be optimized by acting like static objects. Which means meshes are baked so they’re no longer skinned meshes.\nIncluding shadows in the clones avatar would help with realism\nthe gif is my friend showcasing the mod that formerly did these things.",
